cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ControlGate, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ControlGate: NIST SP 800-53 compliance gate for pre-commit and CI"
abstract: >-
  ControlGate is a command-line tool that scans code changes against NIST
  SP 800-53 Rev. 5 security controls before commit and merge. It parses the
  staged diff, a pull request diff or a full repository, runs 18 pattern-based
  security gates (secrets, cryptography, IAM, supply chain, infrastructure as
  code, input validation, audit, change control, dependencies, API, privacy,
  resilience, incident response, observability, memory safety, licenses,
  AI/ML and containers), maps each finding to a NIST control, filters findings
  by the selected NIST or FedRAMP baseline, and returns a BLOCK, WARN or PASS
  verdict as JSON, Markdown or SARIF. It runs as a pre-commit hook, in CI and
  as a GitHub Actions workflow.
authors:
